Also from k368: warn_unlisted_failed_ocpnodes (CR.pm) is never counted in {_apply_warnings} (its caller Apply/Drift.pm:616 drops the return), so a Failed OCPNode not in ocp.yaml leaves the banner without WITH WARNINGS. Whether it should count is a maintainer question (recommendation: count it).

Each is either moved to STDERR with its test, or named as a deliberate exception on this card (the rule asks for exceptions in a ticket). Some may need a decision (the arch warning is a narrative line by design?).



Maintainer decision (Getty, 2026-11-08, hub decision page): (1) every [WARN] line listed on this card goes to STDERR, the robocop arch warning included, each with its test; no exceptions. (2) warn_unlisted_failed_ocpnodes counts in {_apply_warnings}: a Failed OCPNode not in ocp.yaml makes the banner WITH WARNINGS. Build after the release.
